        <h2>Overview</h2>
        <p>Saadani National Park is the only wildlife sanctuary in East Africa where the coastal savanna wilderness directly touches the turquoise Indian Ocean. Located directly across the Zanzibar Channel, it offers the quickest safari access from the archipelago — reached in just a 15-minute flight from Zanzibar Airport or a scenic 1-hour coastal speedboat voyage.</p>
        <p>Experience open-sided 4x4 game drives tracking elephants, giraffes, buffaloes, and lions, paired with an unforgettable river safari along the mangrove-fringed Wami River among pods of hippos and basking Nile crocodiles.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="tour-section">
        <h2>What to Expect</h2>
        <ul class="expect-list">
          <li><strong>Quickest Mainland Access:</strong> Just 15 minutes by light aircraft from ZNZ Airport or 60–90 minutes by scheduled coastal speedboat.</li>
          <li><strong>Bush Meets the Beach:</strong> Spot wildlife wandering along palm-fringed sands and coastal salt pans.</li>
          <li><strong>4x4 Open Vehicle Game Drive:</strong> Explore savanna plains with licensed TANAPA guides spotting elephants, giraffes, zebras, waterbucks, and birdlife.</li>
          <li><strong>Wami River Boat Safari:</strong> Cruise tranquil river reaches to view resident hippos, large crocodiles, and vibrant kingfishers and fish eagles.</li>
          <li><strong>Full Day or Overnight Options:</strong> Return to your Zanzibar beach resort by sunset or extend into a luxury tented lodge overnight stay.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="tour-section">
